  "notes": "The CMS data.cms.gov API works with no login. It returns national rows for PLA codes such as 0340U, which is the Natera Signatera MRD code; it has one rendering provider, the lab. Two limits: (1) The Physician & Other Practitioners file is Medicare fee-for-service Part B only. It undercounts lab volume (Medicare Advantage and commercial are excluded). Counts under 11 are suppressed, so codes with tiny volumes are missing. (2) I could not verify which year each dataset UUID holds. The rows carry no year field, and the catalog pages conflict. UUID 6fea9d79... is the data-api 'latest' endpoint. UUID ddee9e22... is labelled 2023-12-31 in one catalog entry. The two versions are probably consecutive years, most likely 2022 and 2023, but that is unconfirmed. Read the per-year labels on the data.cms.gov dataset page before citing these numbers by year. I did not pull 2021 or 2024. Codes 0364U (clonoSEQ), 81415-81417 and 81427 did not appear in either version, or were suppressed because counts were below 11. 81425 appeared only at tiny volumes (13 and 131 services). The two versions differ for 0340U (Signatera): 13,783 services / 7,028 beneficiaries in the older version vs 25,746 / 11,922 in the newer one. That is +87% in services and +70% in beneficiaries. Services per beneficiary rose from 1.96 to 2.16, and the average Medicare payment fell from $3,838 to $3,519 (-8%). Medicare FFS volume for the main MRD test is therefore still growing very fast, which cuts against a near-term MRD slowdown. It is test counts, not Gb. Signatera's CLFS rate was $3,920 in 2025 and was cut to $3,590 from Jan 2026 (rate cut already known).",
